  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Mu Geminorum",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Gemini",
    "summary": "Mu Geminorum or μ Geminorum, formally named Tejat, is a single star in the northern constellation of Gemini. From parallax measurements obtained during the Hipparcos mission, it is roughly 230 light-years distant from the Sun. The position of the star near the ecliptic means that it is subject to lunar occultations.",
    "intro": "Mu Geminorum or μ Geminorum, formally named Tejat (), is a single star in the northern constellation of Gemini. From parallax measurements obtained during the Hipparcos mission, it is roughly 230 light-years (71 parsecs) distant from the Sun. The position of the star near the ecliptic means that it is subject to lunar occultations.\nMu Geminorum, together with UCAC2 39641417 nearly two arc-minutes away, form a double star designated WDS J06230+2231.  UCAC2 39641417 is itself a binary pair, with the two stars less than an arc-second apart.",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mu_Geminorum",
